{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And his eyes grew dim.</b> As happened to Eli, who did not rebuke his sons, as it says: וְלֹא כִהָה בָּם (I Samuel 3:13), and it is said of him: וְעֵינָיו קָמָה וְלֹא יָכוֹל לִרְאוֹת (I Samuel 4:15). This did not happen to Abraham and Jacob, who were older than Isaac was then and older than Eli was. Of Abraham it is written: וַיֹּסֶף אַבְרָהָם וַיִּקַּח אִשָּׁה (Genesis 25:1), and of Jacob, despite all his troubles and the tears of his eyes, it is written: וַיַּרְא יִשְׂרָאֵל אֶת בְּנֵי יוֹסֵף (Genesis 48:8), even though his vision was heavy, as it says: וְעֵינֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל כָּבְדוּ מִזֹּקֶן (Genesis 48:10), such that he could not recognize the particular likeness."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:31:56.618855945Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}